NNAAMMEE
     wwllaann__ccccmmpp — AES-CCMP crypto support for 802.11 devices

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddeevviiccee wwllaann__ccccmmpp

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The wwllaann__ccccmmpp module handles the AES-CCMP cryptographic requirements of
     the WPA and 802.11i protocols.  It does encapsulation and decapsulation
     of CCMP-encoded 802.11 frames and optionally calculates the AES-CCMP ci‐
     pher.  The wwllaann__ccccmmpp module is an 802.11 cryptographic plugin module for
     use by the wlan(4) module.  This module is automatically loaded if an
     AES-CCMP key is configured; typically by a WPA supplicant program such as
     wpa_supplicant, or a WPA authenticator program such as hhoossttaappdd.  Should
     the underlying network device not be capable of doing the AES-CCMP calcu‐
     lations in hardware, the wwllaann__ccccmmpp module will do the work.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     wlan(4), wlan_tkip(4), wlan_wep(4)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     More information can be found in the IEEE 802.11, WPA, and 802.11i Stan‐
     dards.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The wwllaann__ccccmmpp driver first appeared in FreeBSD 6.0.

